<speak>
<s>This is your Jumu'ah briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">24042026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Washington has authorized lethal fire against suspected mine-layers in the Strait of Hormuz... a shoot-on-sight rule covering unidentified small craft in international waters during an active ceasefire.</s> <s>The Pentagon told Congress that mine clearance could take six months, while Iran denies placing them and Brent crude settled near ninety-eight dollars on Tuesday.</s> <s>A waterway that moves a fifth of the world's oil is now governed by a standing kill order.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Washington brokered a three-week extension of the Lebanon ceasefire, one day after Israeli strikes killed a journalist in the south.</s> <s>Israel still holds a strip of southern Lebanese territory between five and ten kilometres deep, and Lebanese authorities say Israeli operations have killed nearly two thousand five hundred people since early March.</s> <s>It's a patch, not a settlement — and Tel Aviv has already said what comes next.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israeli Defence Minister Israel Katz vowed to destroy Iran's power grid and said the IDF has targets set, awaiting American authorization to resume strikes.</s> <s>Tehran activated air defences that evening, and ceasefire talks hosted by Pakistan remain frozen.</s> <s>The same statement reads as routine in Tel Aviv and as open escalation in Karachi and Singapore.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Qouzah, a Lebanese couple learned their home had been demolished not from the army and not from their municipality, but from a commercial satellite image.</s> <s>Israel razed nearly a third of the village's buildings between early March and mid-April, and UN figures put displacement across Lebanon at one point two million people.</s> <s>Open-source imagery is now how the dispossessed confirm their own dispossession.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>An Egyptian court rejected writer Ahmed Douma's appeal, recycling him into another fifteen-day remand cycle, three years after he completed his last sentence.</s> <s>His lawyers argued that none of the conditions in Egypt's Criminal Procedures Code for pre-trial detention apply to him.</s> <s>Cairo's rotating-case device has quietly converted acquittal-bound defendants into permanent detainees.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Washington reportedly told Seoul to shield the chief executive of Coupang from prosecution or lose access to high-level defence talks.</s> <s>The retailer's breach of thirty-three point seven million accounts has stalled nuclear submarine discussions and intelligence sharing between the allies.</s> <s>A consumer data leak has become a host-nation sovereignty test.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Foreign ministers from Jordan and seven other Muslim-majority states issued a joint statement rejecting any change to the legal status quo at Al-Aqsa.</s> <s>The governments reaffirmed Hashemite custodianship as the binding legal claim, after repeated settler incursions into the compound.</s> <s>Israel hasn't responded, and the statement named no enforcement mechanism.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The US Treasury sanctioned a sitting Cambodian senator, Kok An, and twenty-eight associates for running pig-butchering scam compounds.</s> <s>It's the first time Washington has named a sitting senator under this authority, and Phnom Penh hasn't said whether it'll act.</s> <s>These compounds now stretch across much of Southeast Asia.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Japan's core consumer prices rose one point eight percent in March, before the full oil shock from the Iran war has reached consumers.</s> <s>Japan imports nine out of every ten barrels of oil through the Strait of Hormuz, and central bank data show ocean freight costs jumped more than forty percent in the same month.</s> <s>The Bank of Japan meets on Tuesday, and analysts say a June rate hike is now in play.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Donald Trump threatened Britain with tariffs unless London drops its two-percent digital services tax on American tech revenues.</s> <s>The warning came days before King Charles is due in Washington, and no tariff rate was specified.</s> <s>If it holds, it's the template for killing every other tax that OECD-aligned states have built to reach extraterritorial tech profits.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Australia's Prime Minister Anthony Albanese confirmed his government won't impose a gas export levy that the Australia Institute estimates could raise seventeen billion dollars a year.</s> <s>Independent senator David Pocock called it "caving to gas companies," as domestic prices spike on the back of the Iran war.</s> <s>The world's second-largest LNG exporter has again declined to tax what leaves its shores.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Brussels unveiled forty-four actions under a plan called AccelerateEU to blunt the Iran war's price shock on European importers.</s> <s>It puts the extra cost to the bloc at twenty-four billion euros and mandates storage refills, incentives for electricity over gas, and faster renewables tenders.</s> <s>Any tax measure still needs unanimity, which means any single government holds a veto.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A protein fragment known as the Tenomodulin BRICHOS domain reduced tau clumping, synaptic damage, and memory loss in mice bred for tauopathy.</s> <s>Tau aggregation drives Alzheimer's and related neurodegenerative diseases, and BRICHOS domains appear to bind tau and stop it from misfolding.</s> <s>The intravenous delivery worked in mice — no human trial has been scheduled.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Africa's 2025 Green Drop report found only sixty-six of eight hundred and forty-eight wastewater systems functioning properly, down from one hundred and eighteen the year before.</s> <s>Three Johannesburg plants have been disqualified outright, and the water department hasn't set an enforcement timeline.</s> <s>Nearly four hundred systems are now classed as critical, and the rivers are where that failure ends up.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A new study finds that polluted groundwater is flowing directly into Philippine coral reefs through underground channels that surface regulation can't intercept.</s> <s>The Philippines treats only about thirty percent of its wastewater, and the rest seeps out below the coastline.</s> <s>Filipino reefs make up nearly a tenth of the global total, and no authority yet has jurisdiction over what's happening beneath them.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The White House accused China of using tens of thousands of proxy accounts to distill American frontier AI models through mass queries.</s> <s>Model distillation copies behaviour without source-code access, and Anthropic alone logged sixteen million fraudulent Claude exchanges traced to Chinese networks.</s> <s>If the charge holds, it redefines what counts as AI export control when the product being taken is a probability distribution.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India deployed five hundred cameras at its AI summit this week, in a country where Amnesty International says facial recognition already operates in railways and predictive policing without prior assessment or legal safeguard.</s> <s>The government permits deployment before any human-rights review, and there's no accountability law in force.</s> <s>The summit about AI governance ran, in sha'Allah only briefly, on the very infrastructure it was meant to be debating.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>